module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.FibreCycles.EmbeddedPointHypothesis
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.FieldSituation.Base
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.FlatPullback.LocalizationSequence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.FlatPullback.Support

/-!
# Hypothesis (3) of Stacks 02S5 at the embedded points does not suffice

Stacks 02S5 states its third hypothesis for the *embedded* points of `Z ⊆ X ×_S 𝐏¹_S`: "for any
embedded point `ξ` (Divisors, Definition 31.4.1) of `Z` either `ξ ∉ Z₀ ∪ Z_∞` or `δ(ξ) < k`".
Read that way the lemma is false, and this file is the refutation.

The instance is the one the module documentation of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.FibreCycles.EmbeddedPointHypothesis` describes. Take the
Chow situation over a field, `Stacks.Chow.fieldChowSituation K`, with `X = S = Spec K`,
`f = 𝟙`, `k = 0`, and for `Z` the image of the zero section of `𝐏¹_K ⟶ Spec K`, that is the
kernel ideal sheaf `Stacks.Chow.fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K`. Then

* `Z` is isomorphic to `Spec K` over `Spec K`, so every point of `Z` has relative dimension `0`
  and `dim_δ(Z) = 0 ≤ k + 1`;
* `Z₀ = Z` and `Z_∞ = ∅`, so `dim_δ(Z₀) = 0 ≤ k` and `dim_δ(Z_∞) = ⊥ ≤ k`;
* `Z` has one point, which is the generic point of its unique irreducible component, so `Z` has
  no embedded point at all and hypothesis (3) holds vacuously.

All three hypotheses therefore hold. But `[Z₀]₀` is the class of `Spec K` with its
multiplicity, which is nonzero, while `[Z_∞]₀ = 0`, and on `Spec K` no nonzero `0`-cycle is
rationally equivalent to zero: rational equivalence of `0`-cycles is generated by principal
divisors on integral closed subschemes of `δ`-dimension `1`, and every closed subscheme of
`Spec K` has `δ`-dimension `0`. So the conclusion fails.

The clause the source omits is the one `Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent`
consumes, namely the same condition at every *associated* point of `Z`; equivalently, by
`Stacks.Chow.sectionAvoidance_of_isEmbeddedPoint_of_genericPoints`, the embedded-point clause
together with the extra clause `hGeneric` of
`Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedPoint`. In the instance
below the generic point of `Z` does lie on the zero section and has relative dimension `k`, so
`hGeneric` is exactly what fails. Stacks' single use of 02S5, in the proof of Stacks 0FVJ,
verifies the associated-point form, so nothing downstream depends on the weaker reading.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.eq_zero_of_isRationallyEquivalentToZero_fieldChowSituation` — on `Spec K` the
  only `0`-cycle rationally equivalent to zero is the zero cycle. This is where the conclusion
  of 02S5 fails.
* `Stacks.Chow.zeroFiber_ker_zeroSection_eq_bot` and
  `Stacks.Chow.infinityFiber_ker_zeroSection_eq_top` — the two fibres of the image of the zero
  section are the whole base and the empty scheme.
* `Stacks.Chow.not_forall_genericPoint_notMem_range_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme` — the clause the
  source omits is the one that fails for this `Z`.
* `Stacks.Chow.not_forall_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedPoint` — **the refutation**: there
  is no implication from hypotheses (1), (2) and (3) of Stacks 02S5, with (3) read at the
  embedded points, to its conclusion.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02S5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02S5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05AK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05AK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02RW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02RW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FVJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FVJ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### Irreducible components of a subsingleton space -/

/-- In a subsingleton space the closure of a point is an irreducible component: it is the whole
space, which is irreducible because it is a singleton. -/
theorem mem_irreducibleComponents_closure_singleton {Y : Type*} [TopologicalSpace Y]
    [Subsingleton Y] (y : Y) : closure ({y} : Set Y) ∈ irreducibleComponents Y := by
  have hu : ({y} : Set Y) = Set.univ := Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun z => Subsingleton.elim z y
  rw [hu, closure_univ]
  exact ⟨hu ▸ (isIrreducible_singleton : IsIrreducible ({y} : Set Y)),
    fun {t} _ _ => Set.subset_univ t⟩

/-! ### Delta-dimension over the spectrum of a field -/

variable (K : Type u) [Field K]

/-- Over the spectrum of a field the relative dimension of Stacks 02JW vanishes at every point
where the residue field map is bijective: the dimension function is identically zero, and a
bijective residue field map makes the residue field an algebraic — indeed isomorphic —
extension, of transcendence degree zero. -/
theorem relativeDimension_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (g : Y ⟶ (fieldChowSituation K).S) (y : Y)
    (hy : Function.Bijective (g.residueFieldMap y).hom) :
    relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation K).dimensionFunction g y = 0 := by
  let _ : Algebra ((fieldChowSituation K).S.residueField (g.base y)) (Y.residueField y) :=
    (g.residueFieldMap y).hom.toAlgebra
  have halg : Algebra.IsAlgebraic ((fieldChowSituation K).S.residueField (g.base y))
      (Y.residueField y) := by
    refine ⟨fun x => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := hy.2 x
    exact hr ▸ isAlgebraic_algebraMap r
  change (fieldChowSituation K).dimensionFunction (g.base y) +
      (Cardinal.toNat (Algebra.trdeg ((fieldChowSituation K).S.residueField (g.base y))
        (Y.residueField y)) : ℤ) = 0
  rw [trdeg_eq_zero]
  simp [fieldDimensionFunction, AlgebraicGeometry.fieldBaseDimensionFunction]

/-- Over the spectrum of a field the identity has relative dimension zero at every point. -/
theorem relativeDimension_id_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero (x : (fieldChowSituation K).S) :
    relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation K).dimensionFunction
      (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) x = 0 :=
  relativeDimension_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero K _ x (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso _)

/-- Every closed subscheme of the spectrum of a field has delta-dimension at most zero. -/
theorem schemeDeltaDimension_le_zero_fieldChowSituation {W : Scheme.{u}}
    (j : W ⟶ (fieldChowSituation K).S) [IsClosedImmersion j] :
    schemeDeltaDimension (fieldChowSituation K) (j ≫ 𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      ≤ ((0 : ℤ) : EInt) :=
  schemeDeltaDimension_le_of_forall_relativeDimension_le (fieldChowSituation K) _ j
    fun w => (relativeDimension_id_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero K (j.base w)).le

/-- **On the spectrum of a field the only `0`-cycle rationally equivalent to zero is the zero
cycle.** Rational equivalence of `0`-cycles is witnessed by a family of integral closed
subschemes of delta-dimension `1` (Stacks 02RW), and `Spec K` has none: every closed subscheme
of it has delta-dimension at most `0`. So the witnessing family is empty and the cycle is the
empty sum.

This is the point at which the conclusion of Stacks 02S5 fails for the instance below. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_isRationallyEquivalentToZero_fieldChowSituation
    (α : CycleGroup (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) 0)
    (hα : IsRationallyEquivalentToZero (fieldChowSituation K)
      (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) 0 α) : α = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨J, W, hW, hDim, hLocal, g, hg⟩ := hα
  have hJ : IsEmpty J := by
    refine ⟨fun j => ?_⟩
    have hle := schemeDeltaDimension_le_zero_fieldChowSituation K (W j).subschemeι
    rw [hDim j] at hle
    exact absurd (WithBotTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle) (by omega)
  refine Subtype.ext (Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.ext fun x => ?_)
  rw [hg x]
  change principalDivisorFamilyCoefficient _ _ W hW g x =
    (0 : AlgebraicCycle (fieldChowSituation K).S ℤ) x
  simp [principalDivisorFamilyCoefficient, finsum_of_isEmpty]

/-- On the spectrum of a field rationally equivalent `0`-cycles are equal. -/
theorem eq_of_rationallyEquivalent_fieldChowSituation
    (α β : CycleGroup (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) 0)
    (h : RationallyEquivalent (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) 0 α β) :
    α = β :=
  sub_eq_zero.mp (eq_zero_of_isRationallyEquivalentToZero_fieldChowSituation K _ h)

/-! ### The two fibres of the image of the zero section -/

/-- **The zero fibre of the image of the zero section is the whole base.** The support of the
kernel of the zero section contains its image, so the preimage of that support along the zero
section is everything; on a reduced base an ideal sheaf with full support is the zero ideal. -/
theorem zeroFiber_ker_zeroSection_eq_bot {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) [IsReduced X] :
    zeroFiber f (zeroSection f).ker = ⊥ := by
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_eq_top_iff, zeroFiber,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  refine le_antisymm le_top fun x _ => ?_
  exact Scheme.Hom.range_subset_ker_support (zeroSection f) ⟨x, rfl⟩

/-- **The infinity fibre of the image of the zero section is empty.** The support of the kernel
of the zero section is the image of the zero section, which is disjoint from the image of the
infinity section, so the preimage of that support along the infinity section is empty; an ideal
sheaf with empty support is the unit ideal. -/
theorem infinityFiber_ker_zeroSection_eq_top {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S) :
    infinityFiber f (zeroSection f).ker = ⊤ := by
  rw [← Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_eq_bot_iff, infinityFiber,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  refine le_antisymm (fun x hx => ?_) bot_le
  have hx' : infinitySection f x ∈
      ((zeroSection f).ker.support : Set (projectiveLineProduct f)) := hx
  rw [Scheme.Hom.support_ker, (isClosed_range_zeroSection f).closure_eq] at hx'
  exact absurd hx' (Set.disjoint_right.mp (disjoint_range_zeroSection_infinitySection f) ⟨x, rfl⟩)

/-! ### The counterexample -/

/-- The closed subscheme `Z ⊆ 𝐏¹_K` which is the image of the zero section, as an ideal sheaf on
`projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (Spec K))`. It is the kernel of the zero section, which is a closed
immersion by `Stacks.Chow.isClosedImmersion_zeroSection`. -/
def fieldZeroSectionSubscheme (K : Type u) [Field K] :
    (projectiveLineProduct (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)).IdealSheafData :=
  (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)).ker

/-- The structure morphism of the image of the zero section is an isomorphism: the zero section
is a closed immersion, so it identifies `Spec K` with its image, and the composite of that
identification with the structure morphism is the identity. -/
instance isIso_familyBase_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme :
    IsIso (familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)) := by
  have h : (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)).toImage ≫
      familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K) =
      𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S := by
    simp [familyBase, fieldZeroSectionSubscheme, ← Category.assoc]
  have _ : IsIso ((zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)).toImage ≫
      familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)) := by
    rw [h]; infer_instance
  exact IsIso.of_isIso_comp_left (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)).toImage
    (familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K))

/-- The image of the zero section in `𝐏¹_K` has at most one point. -/
instance subsingleton_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme :
    Subsingleton (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme :=
  (familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
    (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)).isEmbedding.injective.subsingleton

/-- The image of the zero section in `𝐏¹_K` has relative dimension zero at every point. -/
private theorem relativeDimension_familyBase_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme_eq_zero
    (ζ : (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme) :
    relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation K).dimensionFunction
      (familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)) ζ = 0 :=
  relativeDimension_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero K _ ζ (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso _)

/-- The image of the zero section has no embedded point: it has a single point, which is
therefore the generic point of its unique irreducible component, and by Stacks 05AL an embedded
point is an associated point that is not such a generic point. -/
theorem not_isEmbeddedPoint_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme
    (ζ : (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme) :
    ¬ AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedPoint (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme ζ := by
  have _ : IsLocallyNoetherian (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian
      (familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K))
  intro hζ
  exact ((AlgebraicGeometry.isEmbeddedPoint_iff_not_genericPoint _ ζ).mp hζ).2
    ⟨closure ({ζ} : Set (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme),
      mem_irreducibleComponents_closure_singleton ζ, rfl⟩

/-- The zero fibre of the image of the zero section is the whole of `Spec K`. -/
theorem zeroFiber_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme_eq_bot :
    zeroFiber (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K) = ⊥ :=
  zeroFiber_ker_zeroSection_eq_bot _

/-- The infinity fibre of the image of the zero section is empty. -/
theorem infinityFiber_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme_eq_top :
    infinityFiber (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K) = ⊤ :=
  infinityFiber_ker_zeroSection_eq_top _

/-- **The `0`-cycle of the infinity fibre vanishes**, the fibre being empty. -/
theorem cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_infinityFiber_eq_zero :
    cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      (infinityFiber (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)).subschemeι 0
      = 0 := by
  have hempty : IsEmpty
      (infinityFiber (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)).subscheme :=
    (Scheme.Hom.ker_eq_top_iff_isEmpty _).mp (by
      rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι]
      exact infinityFiber_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme_eq_top K)
  refine Subtype.ext (Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.ext fun x => ?_)
  rw [cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply_eq_zero _ _ _ 0 x (by
    rintro ⟨⟨ξ, -⟩, -⟩; exact hempty.elim ξ)]
  rfl

/-- **The `0`-cycle of the zero fibre does not vanish.** The zero fibre is the whole of
`Spec K`, whose unique point is the generic point of its unique irreducible component and has
relative dimension `0`; the coefficient there is the multiplicity of that component, which is
nonzero on a locally Noetherian scheme. -/
theorem cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_zeroFiber_ne_zero :
    cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme (fieldChowSituation K) (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
      (zeroFiber (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)).subschemeι 0
      ≠ 0 := by
  set Z := fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K
  set F := zeroFiber (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) Z
  have hbot : F = ⊥ := zeroFiber_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme_eq_bot K
  have _ : Subsingleton F.subscheme := F.subschemeι.isEmbedding.injective.subsingleton
  obtain ⟨ξ, -⟩ : (default : (fieldChowSituation K).S) ∈ Set.range F.subschemeι := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι, hbot]
    exact Set.mem_univ _
  have _ : IsLocallyNoetherian F.subscheme :=
    LocallyOfFiniteType.isLocallyNoetherian (F.subschemeι ≫ 𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)
  have hξ : ξ ∈ genericPoints F.subscheme := mem_irreducibleComponents_closure_singleton ξ
  intro hzero
  have hcoeff := cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_apply (fieldChowSituation K)
    (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) F.subschemeι 0 ⟨ξ, hξ⟩
    (relativeDimension_id_fieldChowSituation_eq_zero K _)
  have hcast : (componentMultiplicity F.subschemeι ⟨ξ, hξ⟩ : ℤ) = 0 := by
    rw [← hcoeff, hzero]; rfl
  exact componentMultiplicity_ne_zero F.subschemeι ⟨ξ, hξ⟩ (by exact_mod_cast hcast)

/-- **The clause the source omits is exactly the one that fails here.** The unique point of `Z`
is the generic point of its unique irreducible component and has relative dimension `k = 0`, and
it lies on the zero section, `Z` being the image of that section. So the extra clause `hGeneric`
of `Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedPoint` is false for
this `Z`, which is why the corrected statement is untouched by the counterexample below. -/
theorem not_forall_genericPoint_notMem_range_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme :
    ¬ ∀ ζ : (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme,
        ζ ∈ genericPoints (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subscheme →
        relativeDimension (fieldChowSituation K).dimensionFunction
          (familyBase (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K)) ζ = 0 →
        ((fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subschemeι ζ ∉
            Set.range (zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S)) ∧
          (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subschemeι ζ ∉
            Set.range (infinitySection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S))) := by
  intro h
  have hmem : zeroSection (𝟙 (fieldChowSituation K).S) (default : (fieldChowSituation K).S) ∈
      Set.range (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K).subschemeι := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι]
    exact Scheme.Hom.range_subset_ker_support _ ⟨default, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨ζ, hζ⟩ := hmem
  exact (h ζ (mem_irreducibleComponents_closure_singleton ζ)
    (relativeDimension_familyBase_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme_eq_zero K ζ)).1 ⟨default, hζ.symm⟩

/-- **Stacks 02S5 is false with hypothesis (3) read at the embedded points, as the source states
it.** There is no implication from

1. `dim_δ(Z) ≤ k + 1`,
2. `dim_δ(Z₀) ≤ k` and `dim_δ(Z_∞) ≤ k`,
3. every embedded point of `Z` either misses both distinguished sections or has relative
   dimension below `k`,

to `[Z₀]_k ∼_rat [Z_∞]_k`.

The witness is the Chow situation over a field with `X = S = Spec K`, `f = 𝟙`, `k = 0` and
`Z = Stacks.Chow.fieldZeroSectionSubscheme K` the image of the zero section. All three
hypotheses hold — (3) vacuously, by
`Stacks.Chow.not_isEmbeddedPoint_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme` — while `[Z₀]₀ ≠ 0 = [Z_∞]₀` and no
two distinct `0`-cycles on `Spec K` are rationally equivalent, by
`Stacks.Chow.eq_of_rationallyEquivalent_fieldChowSituation`.

The hypothesis the source omits is the one
`Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent` consumes, at every *associated* point of
`Z`; the corrected statement of the tag is
`Stacks.Chow.cycleAssociatedToFibres_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedPoint`, whose extra clause
`hGeneric` is what fails here. -/
theorem not_forall_rationallyEquivalent_of_isEmbeddedPoint :
    ¬ ∀ (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType f] (k : ℤ)
        (Z : (projectiveLineProduct f).IdealSheafData),
      (∀ ζ : Z.subscheme, relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ ≤ k + 1) →
      schemeDeltaDimension C ((zeroFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt) →
      schemeDeltaDimension C ((infinityFiber f Z).subschemeι ≫ f) ≤ (k : EInt) →
      (∀ ζ : Z.subscheme, AlgebraicGeometry.IsEmbeddedPoint Z.subscheme ζ →
        ((Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (zeroSection f) ∧
            Z.subschemeι ζ ∉ Set.range (infinitySection f)) ∨
          relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase f Z) ζ < k)) →
      RationallyEquivalent C f k
        (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C f (zeroFiber f Z).subschemeι k)
        (cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C f (infinityFiber f Z).subschemeι k) := by
  intro h
  refine cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_zeroFiber_ne_zero (ULift.{u} ℚ) ?_
  rw [eq_of_rationallyEquivalent_fieldChowSituation (ULift.{u} ℚ) _ _
    (h (fieldChowSituation (ULift.{u} ℚ)) _ (𝟙 _) 0 (fieldZeroSectionSubscheme (ULift.{u} ℚ))
      (fun ζ => by
        rw [relativeDimension_familyBase_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme_eq_zero (ULift.{u} ℚ) ζ]
        omega)
      (schemeDeltaDimension_le_zero_fieldChowSituation (ULift.{u} ℚ) _)
      (schemeDeltaDimension_le_zero_fieldChowSituation (ULift.{u} ℚ) _)
      (fun ζ hζ =>
        absurd hζ (not_isEmbeddedPoint_fieldZeroSectionSubscheme (ULift.{u} ℚ) ζ)))]
  exact cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_infinityFiber_eq_zero (ULift.{u} ℚ)

end Stacks.Chow

end
